#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064245 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064099 :question/id #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" :question/math-academy-id "e-491" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\left(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7}\\right)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050101 :topic/difficulty 1.7766990018568227 :topic/id #uuid "2d31fc2e-19fe-50d4-bccf-d60b3f5db5c4" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096655} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096656}] :topic/math-academy-id 1112 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048245}] :topic/title "Integrating Exponential Functions Using Linear Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694122 :question-generator/id #uuid "c3e40426-83aa-5c12-9181-236f6db751bc" :question-generator/script "generators/fc/fce84e4448fa45d3a0e3011ac601ded90f7a6eebe9490d6da3467bd5e321899e/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e31ec9-8fca-5231-8200-ca80bc72b044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{3}+\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272940} {:answer/id #uuid "997e80aa-81e0-539a-a4da-c477e354e208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273716} {:answer/id #uuid "c854fd56-2342-58ef-b090-fd79a6ccd523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274128} {:answer/id #uuid "df814db1-8188-5e1b-812c-d9b512f99e8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274359} {:answer/id #uuid "f0053e13-ea2e-5ba8-b9dc-186d83b1f4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "997e80aa-81e0-539a-a4da-c477e354e208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273716} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3e16d2-70ea-5fbe-9bd1-a83494641d8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274842}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d59fc11b-e64a-50a7-ad7d-a5192fdda084" :question/math-academy-id "q-14434" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 6x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 6x{e}^{4x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}-\\int \\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{4x}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064634 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a175a8cb-a6ee-5116-a42e-7718588e0c8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(\\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{x}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061862} {:answer/id #uuid "b04d4f7a-8a20-52a1-b476-c32936814c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(x - 1) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061863} {:answer/id #uuid "da1a54a0-de58-5994-a0ad-8678d8dee9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(1 - \\frac{x}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061864} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8d992b-235f-5112-bb41-ee409c14309a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(x + \\frac{1}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061865} {:answer/id #uuid "638dab82-2814-5689-94e7-12a7d4a7dbd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(x - \\frac{1}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "638dab82-2814-5689-94e7-12a7d4a7dbd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(x - \\frac{1}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061866} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6953c52-54a9-56b3-9aa6-e38c3e7044c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061861}] :question/id #uuid "faff3077-5b5e-5000-bc89-036983a07d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-2425" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\int x2^{x}dx\n$$." :question/worked-solution "Use integration by parts with $u=x$ and $\\mathrm dv=2^x\\,\\mathrm dx$. Then $\\mathrm du=\\mathrm dx$ and $v=2^x/\\ln2$, so\n$$\n\\int x2^x\\,\\mathrm dx=\\frac{x2^x}{\\ln2}-\\frac1{\\ln2}\\int 2^x\\,\\mathrm dx\n=\\frac{2^x}{\\ln2}\\left(x-\\frac1{\\ln2}\\right)+C.\n$$\nDifferentiating the result gives $x2^x$, which verifies the antiderivative."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26da406a-b1ee-533c-8e84-f3f3308fd3a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247767} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} {:answer/id #uuid "b96beb80-9254-5797-a25b-3e85eaa45af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{3{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249082} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8237c1-5f1b-5b27-84a1-36bf62527629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249105} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f75f10-d4ff-5f2b-8f08-23ed364814bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ddb17e-a21a-5bc8-bdfe-e5654290dd4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249710}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a75c4b14-7006-556e-bd1e-e4613f35b446" :question/math-academy-id "q-114287" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f62ef64-e190-59a0-80de-2a8c873c7f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247983} {:answer/id #uuid "81cbaf36-0102-5b7f-97ff-d66d8054c9ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{4}+\\frac{5{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248574} {:answer/id #uuid "99e7a715-8634-5d28-bb4e-237d83c69b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{8}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248798} {:answer/id #uuid "afef77b3-81af-530d-a6f6-eb398f03a3c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249004} {:answer/id #uuid "e249a080-5cfd-59dd-bdec-1e4e038339ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{8x}}{8}+\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afef77b3-81af-530d-a6f6-eb398f03a3c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249004} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a43b96e-f2d9-52db-aaf6-60b9ffaaf8e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249713}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03919aa8-efb9-58ab-8664-d380cf005c1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114288" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{8x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}-\\int \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{8x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022d7b7b-070a-51f5-bd49-94b4db34c49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247437} {:answer/id #uuid "2e34cf00-1e95-5551-a888-a986e9043bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} {:answer/id #uuid "76108c8b-8f42-5f4a-9dd2-e847f09e6e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248463} {:answer/id #uuid "8bfdc77f-bbbe-57f4-9329-f07738aa11a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248678} {:answer/id #uuid "c6440ae3-1132-5195-b3a2-356c7752e48e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e34cf00-1e95-5551-a888-a986e9043bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} :answer-field/id #uuid "eede1f3b-85f2-5008-b473-3fcd59ae080b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250086}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "872e80da-db87-5cbe-89ef-83c58a2b3950" :question/math-academy-id "q-114289" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{3}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & ={3}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{3}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04df1fbb-68fc-5df3-a2f3-5de5f64fbd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247459} {:answer/id #uuid "059681dd-6855-5de5-adb1-fa9432d5314c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{x}{3}-6){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247472} {:answer/id #uuid "19b553b9-fab9-540b-be56-77f1ce0d0a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247659} {:answer/id #uuid "c43e1a7b-f3a2-5b76-a623-7db7da101361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249166} {:answer/id #uuid "ec744b0d-6761-589d-ad26-06e817b26961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{x}{2}-3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04df1fbb-68fc-5df3-a2f3-5de5f64fbd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247459} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3af4228-49fc-5b51-b5a2-20758a8a7ffa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250099}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "623d728c-8114-50ed-8705-4853f0ddb4f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114290" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (x-2){e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (x-2){e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x-2\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{x+3}\\, & ⟹\\,v={e}^{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x-2)\\cdot {e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x-2)\\cdot {e}^{x+3}-\\int {e}^{x+3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-2){e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x-2){e}^{x+3}-\\int {e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-2){e}^{x+3}-{e}^{x+3}+C \\\\  & =(x-3){e}^{x+3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a625e0-f342-5d88-863b-2cc610f12c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x-1){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247918} {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} {:answer/id #uuid "4d558edc-f058-5d64-aa0f-acff177c0e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-3x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248117} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa27907-71bc-5690-9d5a-5ea98a3a03cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248503} {:answer/id #uuid "cd15176c-1580-5959-a4f3-0332eefaf817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2-x){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} :answer-field/id #uuid "f37b9f98-70f3-5724-8992-60b01c3a21f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250097}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1022e01f-7a5a-562e-a877-5ba5b3c9edd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114293" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x-4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x-4)\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x-4)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-3){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271f180d-3faa-5476-a054-bf22f99176bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257122} {:answer/id #uuid "4d6abd70-33c0-5278-82e7-159c499aad7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}+{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257447} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef47045-065b-557c-a1cb-f734f625b80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258180} {:answer/id #uuid "b34f8ff6-8e7b-5a4a-b1de-16e75dced547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-x}-3x{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258342} {:answer/id #uuid "d29bd4f3-02bb-5eb5-b6ba-5b257eab8b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ef47045-065b-557c-a1cb-f734f625b80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258180} :answer-field/id #uuid "47fd06f4-4187-5190-9ee6-b13410e9fa3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259160}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a4ea9ed-1853-52ed-ab6f-46794d76e304" :question/math-academy-id "q-12462" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})-\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-3x{e}^{-x}+3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b012af-7da3-57e7-b3fe-ad695b25321d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257210} {:answer/id #uuid "394ffebc-fc15-59d2-b922-cf67e8668a24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257288} {:answer/id #uuid "98f26b34-1c20-50e4-ae9f-0696b345d0e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258130} {:answer/id #uuid "dee11791-9fa1-5f13-86b4-6751c7ac156e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258723} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7bf65f-10a0-5fb7-85b0-318f615112d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30b012af-7da3-57e7-b3fe-ad695b25321d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257210} :answer-field/id #uuid "4626c1aa-c3c9-5543-a9d9-8d0984251445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259158}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d57f8c60-94ea-5515-8561-35af7ac97700" :question/math-academy-id "q-12556" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}\\right)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "236b60cf-ff8d-5674-870b-bcaaf8d37985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{5x}}{5}+\\frac{3x{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257078} {:answer/id #uuid "4d557db5-ba1a-5b05-b356-74912875cd91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}+\\frac{3x{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257446} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1550eb-3fe9-5df7-a495-0e900c02c6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{25}-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257606} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffe0799-f21d-5fea-a233-c69798ab78fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257623} {:answer/id #uuid "92ec0b8f-683f-538a-921f-014ccb202f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x{e}^{-5x}}{25}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ffe0799-f21d-5fea-a233-c69798ab78fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257623} :answer-field/id #uuid "793c5074-4fab-55cd-94b8-d8144c552545" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259236}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a269e9e4-ba48-5393-8b91-051e5b1bc073" :question/math-academy-id "q-12559" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (3x+5){e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (3x+5){e}^{-5x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x+5\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-5x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x+5)\\cdot {e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x+5)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5}\\right)-\\int \\left(-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5}\\right)\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x+5){e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}\\int {e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109d035c-6ffc-56c3-8581-53bca2233532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256935} {:answer/id #uuid "209845fa-bfdf-5169-8a21-91e5d6fa04ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257046} {:answer/id #uuid "5be69881-f41a-506d-a346-ccfa892bacb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257582} {:answer/id #uuid "6a4a072e-05a9-58e4-83e0-911e978158f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257721} {:answer/id #uuid "a0da683e-5345-5b81-9094-abd5ff0ec151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a4a072e-05a9-58e4-83e0-911e978158f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257721} :answer-field/id #uuid "b284ab05-c542-58e4-99b1-8ce31da489d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259344}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b258b659-45f7-5842-b37a-ee530a2eb1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-12560" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+7)\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+7)\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c795865-da64-5e14-9024-3c7c02d718c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288124} {:answer/id #uuid "51fe0db3-d702-5875-904d-f79bd58f19bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288600} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5a066a-1db0-5b07-b438-285b415f19bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288802} {:answer/id #uuid "9611c013-b6fd-5217-9d39-883aca3329d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289037} {:answer/id #uuid "c91e7928-ce32-56f4-8b9f-43257961903a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e5a066a-1db0-5b07-b438-285b415f19bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288802} :answer-field/id #uuid "94c0f155-a00b-507b-a0ba-cb1120435b6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290061}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00c040ca-17ee-59e4-9387-a983daa9bae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-2420" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{5}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={5}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\frac{{5}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fea6d91-968c-5f4d-8499-0425dc5d7fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(3x+2){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362862} {:answer/id #uuid "df58de38-7310-5f19-9844-03c75ef49b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362863} {:answer/id #uuid "f721fccd-de41-549f-b75e-093592b0c032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+4){e}^{3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362864} {:answer/id #uuid "7db9ef7b-e876-5195-b2bc-5e90b186c364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(4x-3){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362865} {:answer/id #uuid "cab8da55-0308-5e36-8634-1b58557947b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(4x-1){e}^{3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df58de38-7310-5f19-9844-03c75ef49b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362863} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bcef777-2395-5b4a-81aa-40676383c492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362861}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd0da194-e627-59a2-b874-56e9ce11e475" :question/math-academy-id "q-114291" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (2x+1)\\cdot {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(2x+1)\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(2x+1){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{9}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba8cff6-a436-587b-947b-b845d40cdf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362998} {:answer/id #uuid "0bf7139d-5b6a-513e-8c05-ea38b19064dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\frac{3x{e}^{2x}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362999} {:answer/id #uuid "1a22e02f-c34e-55ad-b5ee-acd29d97566a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363000} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c30e70-a737-5f41-9c71-a8d0f2188c7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a00544-29af-5a0e-9dbd-8c18e64ae108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3c30e70-a737-5f41-9c71-a8d0f2188c7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4e46148-8029-5a37-a794-c93ccb0b0139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362997}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "708f4971-ac44-5610-9dca-92afa6cd2300" :question/math-academy-id "q-12558" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186582409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b554e5-67f5-59cc-b410-930af877330a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581881} {:answer/id #uuid "120160f0-0063-52a3-bcb3-6e68643ff806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581884} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf32d90-eb55-5cb6-bd84-8a7cc555ceef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581983} {:answer/id #uuid "adfe33aa-5eaf-5562-b5a2-6cf71f2466e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582112} {:answer/id #uuid "da6d045c-c0e4-5deb-99cd-c404c3cf45bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}+\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adfe33aa-5eaf-5562-b5a2-6cf71f2466e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582112} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a94088-6e0b-5425-b352-4fdea86a8ff4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186582268}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecef7e80-ec65-5fcc-bcee-fa246b15e720" :question/math-academy-id "q-14439" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{5x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{5x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{5x}}{5}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {e}^{5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{5x}}{5}-\\frac{{e}^{5x}}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608215 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a61ad7-79c1-597e-b11c-19dd09903bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607829} {:answer/id #uuid "371c726f-d93e-535e-8a96-08a8cf95914f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}+\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607867} {:answer/id #uuid "e977e102-a296-5ad5-ac58-227bccc1a06d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608060} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1ae4d5-c8d6-5a8d-84e5-ae8b3f0a3d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608064} {:answer/id #uuid "fc91c68d-0d4b-50b6-a510-3e9c2f09fe7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15a61ad7-79c1-597e-b11c-19dd09903bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607829} :answer-field/id #uuid "18e8c34f-a0b9-520d-9f5e-f104314fae97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608094}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad8a7bb6-4f28-5469-bc34-0461c89c315f" :question/math-academy-id "q-14454" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x{e}^{6x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{6x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{6x}}{6}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{1}{6}\\int {e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{6x}}{6}-\\frac{{e}^{6x}}{36}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d0b42a-bcf4-51c6-ab54-7d619fcc4415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 x e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694093} {:answer/id #uuid "703ccc68-e8bb-50fb-a709-7a06443daab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12 x e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694103} {:answer/id #uuid "94a32af5-4019-5d4b-8c8a-eaf31851e7a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 x e^{- x} - 6 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694107} {:answer/id #uuid "9b7679ab-d43d-57be-b79e-6b6ee74770fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 x e^{- x} + 6 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694109} {:answer/id #uuid "fa03e39a-50ff-56c3-b9ea-68b9aff83c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 x e^{- x} - 6 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa03e39a-50ff-56c3-b9ea-68b9aff83c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 x e^{- x} - 6 e^{- x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694121} :answer-field/id #uuid "74250762-f401-5a87-8f36-2ce48593ca34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14bea470-184c-5ecf-9f29-5ddeabc665f9" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =6 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{- x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=- e^{- x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6 x\\cdot e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6 x\\cdot (- e^{- x})-\\int (- e^{- x})\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6 xe^{- x}+6\\cdot \\int e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 xe^{- x}+6\\cdot \\int e^{- x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6 xe^{- x}-6\\cdot e^{- x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{- x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =-6 x e^{- x} - 6 e^{- x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694090 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43f17e0b-6268-57e2-b958-be505667edba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} + \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694099} {:answer/id #uuid "6691ac63-0715-5aa8-beda-5e6f73f58a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694102} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ec7872-591d-54b6-8518-d1e7ab3fe837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}} + \\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694114} {:answer/id #uuid "c6dd5d6e-cc9c-5f8c-b55c-33653930fb6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694115} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f8a7cc-fe5a-541c-af1c-c1dae3c73035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6691ac63-0715-5aa8-beda-5e6f73f58a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a26a53b2-9ce2-5c2a-a9de-7dfb9416db7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694111}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19e99f60-9da4-54ea-bd6c-9fe3cc030a8c" :question/problem "$$\n\\int x3^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x3^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =3^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot 3^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}-\\int \\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x3^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3^{x} x}{\\ln{(3 )}}-\\int \\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}}\\cdot x3^{x}-\\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\cdot 3^{x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3^{x}}{\\ln{(3 )}}(x - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x3^{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\left(\\frac{x}{\\ln{(3 )}} - \\frac{1}{\\ln{(3 )}^{2}}\\right)3^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 