{:answer/id #uuid "32beccaa-15e1-5fa9-b88f-aa9382ec8ddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} + \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694096} {:answer/id #uuid "a008af24-7ddd-5827-914c-fd63d76d869c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} + \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694110} {:answer/id #uuid "deb81a55-59e3-518e-8374-0057bfba1a84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} - \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deb81a55-59e3-518e-8374-0057bfba1a84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} - \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694118} :answer-field/id #uuid "2be87ee8-ca80-5505-95e9-3e74dd2a5fe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694095}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95e9ca22-58f3-5e64-8045-179bb6e51fff" :question/problem "$$\n\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =6 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{7 x - 4}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{e^{7 x - 4}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6 x\\cdot e^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x & =6 x\\cdot \\frac{e^{7 x - 4}}{7}-\\int \\frac{e^{7 x - 4}}{7}\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 6 xe^{7 x - 4}-\\frac{6}{7}\\cdot \\int e^{7 x - 4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 6 xe^{7 x - 4}-\\frac{6}{49}\\cdot e^{7 x - 4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6 xe^{7 x - 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\frac{6 x e^{7 x - 4}}{7} - \\frac{6 e^{7 x - 4}}{49}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88048e6a-2f70-5035-a493-7b95701c52d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} + \\frac{4 e^{6 x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694123} {:answer/id #uuid "b29dae9c-35ba-5e46-85ed-752de6431d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} + \\frac{2 e^{6 x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694124} {:answer/id #uuid "cb1d0419-dae4-5f8d-a936-85024d60a873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{2 e^{6 x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694126} {:answer/id #uuid "d2fba22b-7740-50b8-ac40-90d9be311fdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{4 e^{6 x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694127} {:answer/id #uuid "edf1ad24-151a-5ed7-90dd-37805a6c88ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{e^{6 x}}{36}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb1d0419-dae4-5f8d-a936-85024d60a873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{2 e^{6 x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694126} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc41504-9ae9-5c53-8698-b5f4f258019b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694128}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7c08dd9-661c-5fb8-b272-6f01e9991cca" :question/problem "$$\n\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =8 x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=8 \\\\ {v}^{′} & =e^{6 x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{e^{6 x}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 8 x\\cdot e^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =8 x\\cdot \\frac{e^{6 x}}{6}-\\int \\frac{e^{6 x}}{6}\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 8 xe^{6 x}-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\int e^{6 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 8 xe^{6 x}-\\frac{2}{9}\\cdot e^{6 x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCollecting the linear terms gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8 xe^{6 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\frac{4 x e^{6 x}}{3} - \\frac{2 e^{6 x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}]}
